      "title": "Read me first",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 1 - Write a prompt\n\nTurns one line of an idea into a full MiniMax-H3 audio-video description:\nshot list, camera moves, the soundscape and the music.\n\n## What it needs\n\nOne small language model, fetched on the first run. `Qwen3.5-4B` is a\n2.6 GB download and writes inside about 5 GB of VRAM. Nothing to install.\n\n**No MiniMax-H3 video checkpoint is involved here.** This template only\nwrites the text. The generator is in templates 5 and 6.\n\n## How to use it\n\n1. Put a short idea into **prompt**. One sentence is enough.\n2. Set **duration** to the length of the clip you are going to make --\n   in both nodes. The shot list is built to fill exactly that.\n3. Run. The finished prompt comes out on the right.\n\nA bigger card writes better prose: **model** holds a 9B, a 12B and\nseveral 27B quants in the same list.\n\n## What the second node is for\n\n**Prompt Check** loads nothing and generates nothing. It reads the\nfinished text against the rules the H3 guides are written by -- shot\nnumbering, cut times against the duration, dialogue markup, reference\ntags -- and reports what it found. It never edits anything: what goes\nin comes out of `prompt` untouched, so it can sit anywhere in a graph.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- **2 - Rewrite a prompt with the 27B LoRA** -- the LightX2V adapter\n  this pack is named after, for a 16 GB card and up.\n- **3 - Write a prompt from references** -- when the shot has to match\n  pictures you already have.\n- **4 - Ready-made prompts** -- a thousand finished ones, no model at all.\n- **5 - Prompt to video** -- this writer wired into MiniMax-H3 itself."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
